Removes both halves of draft 60's directory rule (§8.3 step 2). The
keep-the-directory rule is judged only when the revert runs, not again
as the directory's move would be dispatched (`keep_directories`), and a
create beneath a directory whose move to the trash is pending no longer
waits for it (`want::gates`). A want for a live entry that appears
beneath the directory after the revert then lands in it, and the move
takes it to the trash.

Since draft 61 the host moves only an empty directory, which refuses the
same move, so no seed of the slices or of 0 to 9,999 fails with this
patch, and the rule's unit tests stand in for one.

test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_directorys_move_yields_at_dispatch_to_a_want_beneath_it
test: delocal-engine folder::tests::a_create_beneath_a_directory_on_its_way_to_the_trash_waits_for_it

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/folder.rs b/crates/engine/src/folder.rs
index 48bed7e..7ae54b7 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/folder.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/folder.rs
@@ -2721,7 +2721,7 @@ impl FolderState {
             self.wants.pause_inbound();
             return (Vec::new(), Vec::new());
         }
-        let mut adopted = self.keep_directories(now);
+        let mut adopted: Vec<IndexRecord> = Vec::new();
         let steps = self.wants.dispatch(now, &self.rules, peers);
         let mut host = Vec::new();
         for step in steps {
diff --git a/crates/engine/src/want.rs b/crates/engine/src/want.rs
index a2662d1..f2d1a57 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/want.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/want.rs
@@ -1310,7 +1310,7 @@ fn gates(want: &Want, other: &Want) -> bool {
         // of a directory above it to the trash until the move is reported
         // or dropped (§8.3 step 2, draft 60), so that nothing lands in a
         // directory on its way to the trash.
-        other.path().is_ancestor_of(want.path()) && (other.is_dir_create() || other.is_trash())
+        other.path().is_ancestor_of(want.path()) && other.is_dir_create()
     }
 }
 
